  "cause": "gdbm_open_ext assigns an existing descriptor without applying the requested close-on-exec flag. Recovery passes its temporary descriptor through this path. The original fdop helper compares the target descriptor number with dup(0), which can miss a leaked higher descriptor. The additional control uses fcntl plus actual fork/exec descriptor inspection.",
  "repair": "Apply F_GETFD/F_SETFD when GDBM_CLOEXEC is requested for a supplied descriptor. Preserve existing flags and the existing GDBM_CLOERROR ownership/error rules. Add a port revision and an authored four-case native regression control; retain all original upstream tests and defaults.",
